   "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
   "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/subscriptions",
   "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/orgs",
   "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/repos",
   "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/events{/privacy}",
   "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/simin-yuan/received_events",
   "type": "User",
   "user_view_type": "public",
   "site_admin": false
  },
  "created_at": "2026-10-19T13:26:14Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-19T13:26:14Z",
  "body": "Thanks for the check. I don't think this is a duplicate of #54285. That issue is about `codex exec --output-schema` with `minLength`/`maxLength` constraints failing on some models. This one asks for a client-side cut when any streamed reply turns into a repetition loop, whatever the schema or model. They meet at one point: the gpt-6-sol run in #54285 produced 216,579 characters of repetitive JSON and was still streaming when that harness's ~600-second diagnostic limit stopped it. That run is the kind of output this request is about, so I'll keep this open as a separate request.\n",
